Dear Yihui,

I have used your hack and am still quite fond of it. However, I have discovered that when I set

opts_chunk$set(dev = c('pdf','png'))

and label the figure, say

<<Figure.1.1, out.width='1\\linewidth'>>=

only the pdf figures are renamed "Figure_1_1.pdf", meanwhile the png figures are still named "Figure_1_1-1.pdf".

Any suggestions on how to make the hack apply to png figures as well? Thanks!

# Here's the hack that works on pdf files but not on png files

local({
  hook_plot = knit_hooks$get('plot')
  knit_hooks$set(plot = function(x, options) {
    name = sub('-1([.][a-z]{3,4})$', '\\1', x)
    if (name != x) file.rename(x, name)
    hook_plot(name, options)
  })
})

